\f1\b \cf2 \strokec3 On the overall framing
\f0\b0 \
The "no test set" decision is defensible 
\f3\i if
\f0\i0  you're explicit that the goal is characterizing the data-generating process, not estimating generalization error. But there's still a risk: if you tune hyperparameters aggressively on K-fold CV, your importance estimates may reflect an overfit model. The mitigation is to use a stability check (see below) rather than a held-out set.\
